1
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:06,000
My Christmas Love is a tv movie, romance, comedy film directed by Jeff Fisher.

2
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:06,000
A hopeless romantic who can’t ever seem to give a guy a real chance begins receiving
each of the "12 Days of Christmas” as gifts anonymously at her door.

3
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:06,000
As she tries to figure out who is sending the gifts, she begins to believe that
the mystery suitor could finally live up to her expectations.

4
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:06,000
Cynthia Baker, played by Meredith Hagner.

5
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Liam Pollok, played by Bobby Campo.

6
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Scott Ericson, played by Aaron O'Connell.

7
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Tom Baker, played by Gregory Harrison.

8
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Janet Baker, played by Megan Park.

9
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Roger, played by Ben Gavin.

10
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Love Actually is a 2003 Christmas romantic comedy film
written and directed by Richard Curtis.

11
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
The film features an ensemble cast, composed predominantly of British
actors, many of whom had worked with Curtis in previous projects.

12
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
An international co-production of the United Kingdom, United States
and France, it was mostly filmed on location in London.

13
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
The film delves into different aspects of love as shown through 10 separate stories involving a
variety of individuals, many of whom are interlinked as the plot progresses.

14
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
The story begins five weeks before Christmas and is played out in a weekly countdown
until the holiday, followed by an epilogue that takes place in the New Year.

15
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
The film, Curtis's first as director, was released in the US on 14 November
2003 and a week later in the UK during its theatrical run.

16
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:06,000
Love Actually was a box-office success, grossing $250.2
million worldwide on a budget of $40–45 million.

17
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
The film received mixed reviews and a nomination for the Golden Globe
Award for Best Motion Picture – Musical or Comedy.

18
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
In recent years, it has developed a cult following, and is often a staple film shown
during the Christmas period in both the United Kingdom and United States.

19
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
A made-for-television short sequel, Red Nose Day Actually, aired in two different versions on
BBC One and NBC in 2017, as part of the fundraising event Red Nose Day 2017.

20
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
